public String sortString(String s) {
    if (s == null || s.isEmpty()) {
        return s;
    }
    char[] chars = s.toCharArray();
    Arrays.sort(chars);
    StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
    while (result.length() < chars.length) {
        int minIndex = 0;
        int maxIndex = chars.length - 1;
        while (minIndex < maxIndex) {
            result.append(chars[minIndex]);
            minIndex++;
        }
        while (maxIndex >= 0) {
            result.append(chars[maxIndex]);
            maxIndex--;
        }
    }
    return result.toString();
}
```
This method first sorts the input string using the `Arrays.sort()` method. Then, it iterates over the sorted array of characters and appends the smallest character to the result string, then the second smallest, and so on. After all the smallest characters have been appended, it appends the largest character, then the second largest, and so on. This process is repeated until all characters have been appended to the result string. Finally, the method returns the result string.

Note that this method assumes that the input string is not null or empty. If the input string is null or empty, the method returns the input string as is.

